-- Q12430: Public Company Reporting [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 480-10-S99-3A (SEC Staff guidance), when a redeemable NCI is remeasured to redemption value and the adjustment exceeds the NCI''s share of earnings, the excess reduces income available to common shareholders for EPS purposes, analogous to a preferred dividend. The $200,000 decreases the EPS numerator.
Wrong (A): Although the remeasurement is recorded in equity, SEC guidance requires it to affect the EPS numerator. The adjustment is not neutral for EPS purposes.
Wrong (B): The remeasurement reduces, not increases, income available to common shareholders. It represents value transferred to the NCI holders at the parent''s expense.
Wrong (D): SEC guidance applies to all redeemable NCI remeasurements regardless of whether they arise at the subsidiary level. The adjustment flows through to consolidated EPS.$EXPL$
