-- Q12460: Public Company Reporting [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 260-10-45-12 and ASC 470-20-25-5, accretion of a beneficial conversion feature on preferred stock is treated as a deemed dividend. The $80,000 current-year accretion is deducted from the EPS numerator, reducing income available to common shareholders to $920,000.
Wrong (A): Although the BCF does not affect the income statement, it directly impacts the EPS numerator through the deemed dividend mechanism, just like declared preferred dividends.
Wrong (B): The full $200,000 BCF is not deducted at issuance. The discount is accreted over the period to the earliest conversion date, with only $80,000 recognized in the current year.
Wrong (D): The accretion is deducted from, not added to, the numerator because it represents value transferred to preferred shareholders.$EXPL$
