-- Q12476: Public Company Reporting [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 260-10-45-29 and ASC 718, stock-based compensation expense reduces net income (the numerator), and unvested dilutive awards add incremental shares to the denominator. These are two separate, required effects reflecting different aspects of the arrangement: cost in the numerator and potential dilution in the denominator.
Wrong (A): Excluding RSUs from diluted EPS would understate dilution. The expense and the diluted shares address different dimensions of the compensation arrangement.
Wrong (B): No genuine double-counting exists. The numerator reflects the compensation cost while the denominator reflects potential share issuance, and both are independently required.
Wrong (C): Adding back the expense would eliminate the recognized cost of the award, contrary to ASC 718. The numerator should reflect the compensation charge.$EXPL$
