-- Q14987: Financial Statement Ratios [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Gross profit margin = gross profit / net sales. Gross profit is net sales minus cost of goods sold, per ASC 220-10-45 income statement presentation. For Calloway: ($1,200,000 - $780,000) / $1,200,000 = 35%. This isolates the revenue retained after direct production costs.
Wrong (A): Net income divided by net sales calculates the net profit margin, which includes all expenses beyond cost of goods sold.
Wrong (B): Operating income divided by net sales gives the operating margin, which deducts operating expenses but not interest and taxes.
Wrong (C): Net sales minus operating expenses divided by net sales is not the gross profit margin formula because it deducts SG&A and other operating costs beyond COGS.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14987;

